From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0393-upstream-04-bank-reupload-switch.patch

Source: 0393-upstream-04-bank-reupload-switch.patch
buffer_cache: EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD=2 or 3 re-uploads native uniform banks on every bind

Port of Djihads80/Eglantine 031e07436c and 8b3aff59e4 (kraibse, branch fix/oot-blackscreen,
2026-11-05), at the default 87bd90ae35 settled on. GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

The source commits: Ocarina drew one material pure white for one or two frames every few hundred
presents. Once per frame left per-draw data stale when the game rewrote it between draws. Bursts of a
still camera: 1/500 and 1/690 flashes once per frame, 0/1000 on every bind. Later: not gone in a user
session, and with the byte loads it cost about 8 ms of front-thread time on a 50.4 ms frame, so
87bd90ae35 made once per frame the default again.

0 off, 1 or unset once per frame (this core today, 5c7da2713a), 2 every bind of a 64 KiB bank, 3 every
bind of any native bank.

Changed from the source: the EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS counter is left out (a getenv per re-upload).

For one-frame white flashes only. It does nothing for the steady fog.

Runs on the PS5: same core path. Pool memory: none. Front-thread cost on the console: not measured.

Co-authored-by: kraibse <33869366+kraibse@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 885b806670..c3d17b983b 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -1430,10 +1430,20 @@ void BufferCache<P>::BindHostGraphicsUniformBuffer(size_t stage, u32 index, u32
     // Native programs keep tables next to their code in a 64 KiB bank read with indirect offsets
     // (Splatoon Raiders: the dialogue box corners in c1). Writes to that memory can go unnoticed by
     // the memory tracker, leaving stale host contents, so upload such a bank again once per frame.
-    if (has_host_buffer && (*channel_state->uniform_buffer_sizes)[stage][index] == 0x10000 &&
-        size != 0 && gpu_memory != nullptr && gpu_memory->UsesNativeTiling() &&
-        !memory_tracker.IsRegionGpuModified(device_addr, size) &&
-        native_indirect_uniforms_this_frame.insert(device_addr).second) {
+    // EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD: 0 off, 1 once per frame (unset), 2 every bind of a 64 KiB bank, 3 every
+    // bind of any native bank. Once per frame left Ocarina of Time's per-draw material data stale
+    // for a frame now and then (white flashes); every bind costs front-thread time.
+    static const char bank_mode = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD");
+        return value != nullptr ? value[0] : '1';
+    }();
+    const bool native_bank = has_host_buffer && size != 0 && gpu_memory != nullptr &&
+                             gpu_memory->UsesNativeTiling() &&
+                             !memory_tracker.IsRegionGpuModified(device_addr, size);
+    if (bank_mode != '0' && native_bank &&
+        (bank_mode == '3' || (*channel_state->uniform_buffer_sizes)[stage][index] == 0x10000) &&
+        (bank_mode == '2' || bank_mode == '3' ||
+         native_indirect_uniforms_this_frame.insert(device_addr).second)) {
         // The bank size is only an upper limit: stop at the end of the mapped memory.
         u64 mapped_size = 0;
         while (mapped_size < size &&
